  "paragraph": 34,
  "text": "That leads to the golden rule of long-term harness maintenance. Frontier models improve every few months, so keep a clean architectural line between permanent harness infrastructure and temporary model workarounds. Sandboxes, deterministic verifiers, prompt caching, and trace logs, the core primitives exposed by builder runtimes like the Claude Agent SDK, OpenAI Agents SDK, and LangChain Deep Agents on LangGraph, stay valuable forever. Elaborate chain-of-thought nudges, rigid routers, and JSON repair shims should be modular enough to build to delete the day your evals prove the next generation no longer needs them.",
